            "type": "paragraph",
            "text": "List items can be changed by assigning a new value to an index, and new items can be added with append()."
          },
          {
            "type": "callout",
            "tone": "note",
            "title": "Python code (each .... is one 4-space indent)",
            "text": "fruits = [\"Mango\", \"Apple\", \"Banana\"]\nfruits[0] = \"Orange\"\nfruits.append(\"Pineapple\")\nprint(fruits)    # ['Orange', 'Apple', 'Banana', 'Pineapple']"
          }
        ]
